# Real PayFast export data - contains real members' names, emails, and
# payment amounts. Was committed here as payfastTransactions.json/.csv,
# then (still incorrectly) moved into a tracked SQL migration
# (033_payfast_transactions.sql PART 2) as a "fix" that just relocated the
# same leak - a second PII review caught that and redacted it, moving the
# real data to supabase/.private-history/ below instead. Never let a real
# export like this back into the tracked tree in any format. The
# anonymized src/data/payfastTransactions.mock.json fixture (Mock Admin
# only, fake names/emails) is fine to keep tracked.
src/data/payfastTransactions.json
src/data/payfast_transactions_*.csv
*Transaction_History*.csv

# Real, un-redacted content of one-time historical seed migrations
# (004/012/021/029/033 - see each file's own header comment for what was
# redacted and why). Local-only, disaster-recovery copies - the real data
# already lives in Supabase; these are never meant to be committed or
# re-run against a live database that already has this data.
#
# Any other one-time script involving real member data (e.g. a targeted
# revoke/cleanup) belongs in supabase/.private-scripts/, not a tracked
# migration - run once from the Supabase SQL Editor, then safe to delete
# locally. This is the standing rule going forward, not just how the
# PII incident above got fixed.
supabase/.private-history/
supabase/.private-scripts/
